-- Name: [SCHEMA] T-002 B-04b (v1) - study_sessions cutover: a manual log must carry a classification (CHECK, NOT VALID), behind the set assertion and the closure assertions
--
-- Description: PERSISTENT DDL (one constraint). Implements brief B v10 (0fe77dec72dc) section 4.3 and plan v18 section 5.2 as amended by change-log Entries 24 and 25 (data fix dropped; the closure assertion
-- is "zero sinks" because the allowlist of study_sessions sinks is empty). Tier 1: QA audits this exact file by hash, at most two rounds; the Founder authorizes the run by hash (Gates 2 and 3).
-- Run ONLY after the observation window, the fresh closure re-run (D-03 v11, D-04, D-05) and the final D-07 snapshot are saved and accepted, and after B-04a, B-04a-fix and F1 are live. One selection in the
-- Supabase SQL Editor = ONE transaction. Nothing outside this file's own statements is changed; no row is added, updated or removed.
--
-- WHAT IT DOES, IN ORDER (all in one transaction; any failed assertion raises and NOTHING is applied)
--   0. Pins the session (TimeZone UTC, DateStyle 'ISO, YMD', IntervalStyle iso_8601, extra_float_digits 1) so fingerprints are reproducible; lock_timeout 5 s, statement_timeout 60 s.
--   1. LOCK TABLE public.study_sessions IN ACCESS EXCLUSIVE MODE (no insert can commit between the checks and the rule; held until commit).
--   2. Identity: the 17 live columns equal the frozen list with types; the B-04a constraints (five, NOT VALID), study_sessions_source_check (validated) and the label-guard trigger exist; the new constraint does not.
--   3. Closure (zero sinks, live catalogue): no non-superuser, non-owner role holds UPDATE (table or any column) on study_sessions; PUBLIC holds no UPDATE or INSERT (table or column); anon and service_role have no
--      INSERT, authenticated has INSERT; the only non-internal trigger is trg_study_sessions_label_guard (enabled); no rewrite rule; no view over the table is insertable or updatable; no foreign key whose child is
--      study_sessions has SET NULL or SET DEFAULT; no routine anywhere (any schema outside pg_catalog and information_schema) contains a statement INSERT INTO, UPDATE, MERGE INTO or COPY on study_sessions; no cron job
--      command does (cron.job must be visible). Dynamic SQL and extension routines are covered by the clearance list of the D-03/D-05 closure re-run, which is a precondition recorded in the Gate 3 request, not an
--      assertion of this file.
--   4. Set assertion SA (plan 5.2): the anchor A (1,411 pairs id|fingerprint, the S0 snapshot of 09/10/2026, embedded below; its overall hash and count are asserted first) against C, the current manual rows with a
--      NULL classification, using the same 17-column fingerprint as D-07 v1: (i) no id in C outside A (nothing added); (ii) every id in both has the same fingerprint (nothing altered); anchor ids no longer in C are
--      REPORTED as gone (no row) or classified (row exists, no longer manual/NULL); shrinkage never fails.
--   5. ALTER TABLE ... ADD CONSTRAINT study_sessions_manual_requires_classification CHECK (source <> 'manual' OR classification IS NOT NULL) NOT VALID. NOT VALID on purpose: the legacy rows stay as they are and are never validated; every new INSERT
--      and every UPDATE of a row must satisfy it. Consequence stated (brief B): an UPDATE of a legacy manual/NULL row is refused (no client or service role can UPDATE anyway; the owner can, and is refused too).
--   6. Post-check, then ONE read-only result row (tool_version B04b-v1, counts, hash of C, constraint facts).
--
-- Blind spots, stated: the SQL Editor is one session, so a log saved at the very instant of the cutover is argued from lock semantics (NOT COVERED by test unless a two-connection run is approved); a stale browser
-- tab on the F1 or older bundle that still saves a manual log without a classification will be REFUSED after this runs (the log is not stored) - the Founder's accepted residual; SA proves the stored values equal S0,
-- not who wrote them.
--
-- HOW TO RUN: check docs/database/t002/CURRENT.md first (file name and first 12 characters of the sha256). Select the WHOLE file and click Run once. Expected: one result row; "tool_version":"B04b-v1",
-- "constraint_added":true, "constraint_validated":false, "sa_added":0, "sa_altered":0. Save the result cell unchanged as docs/discussions/evidence/T-002_B04b-SCHEMA-raw_<dd-mm-yyyy>.raw.txt. An error is evidence: save
-- the error text, do not edit and re-run (a lock timeout is the only case to simply re-run at a quiet moment).

SET LOCAL TimeZone = 'UTC';
SET LOCAL DateStyle = 'ISO, YMD';
SET LOCAL IntervalStyle = 'iso_8601';
SET LOCAL extra_float_digits = 1;
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '60s';

LOCK TABLE public.study_sessions IN ACCESS EXCLUSIVE MODE;

DO $b04b$
